1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a day floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off,

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,940
onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:39,160
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I try to chase
some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pathetic, yet one yawn changes nothing.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
the townscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,180
From the pointed hat's water vessel,

9
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sets toward the
sky above the great temple.

10
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow have to end too

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness has been lost.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,480
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it after hearing it.

13
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:52,140
Hey, Grandma.

14
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:55,920
That's why you run out of money,
buying stuff like that.

15
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:59,220
Are you there, Grandma?
I'm taking it without asking!

16
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:00,660
Hey, Grandma.

17
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,680
Hey, if you're there, at least answer!

18
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:11,260
What's with that serious face?

19
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,420
Don't tell me someone has
gone to the afterlife...

20
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,880
It's not that, Ryo-san.

21
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:17,440
Actually...

22
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:39,400
Hahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaha...

23
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,560
There's no need to laugh.

24
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,340
That's right!
Everyone was looking forward to it!

25
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:47,320
Well, it is pitiful, I suppose, but...

26
00:02:48,380 --> 00:02:49,760
Where did that money go?

27
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:54,380
We tried to do something, so everyone
split up and scraped it together, but...

28
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:56,660
The senior citizens' association
has over twenty members, right?

29
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:58,420
It's nowhere near enough!

30
00:02:58,420 --> 00:02:59,500
Right?

31
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:04,160
Alright, leave it to me!

32
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,420
Wait, what?

33
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:09,340
With that money,
I'll take everyone to Hawaii!

34
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,820
Can you really do that?

35
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:12,900
Leave it to me!

36
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:15,320
There's no such thing as
"impossible" in my dictionary!

37
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,670
45, 46, 47,

38
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:20,920
48, 49, 50...

39
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,140
Yay! There's 500,000 yen!

40
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:25,980
That's barely enough for two or three people,
at most.

41
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:28,380
What are you planning to do,
Mister Fisherman?

42
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:31,520
Obviously, we'll ask Nakagawa or Reiko.

43
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,780
Those two are suckers for a good cause, so.

44
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:37,880
They'll take twenty or thirty old ladies to Hawaii,
no problem.

45
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,630
The grandpas and grandmas will be overjoyed,

46
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,840
and I'll pocket 500,000 yen in clear profit.

47
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,900
I figured as much.

48
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:50,440
What? Nakagawa and Reiko aren't even here!

49
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,602
Yeah, apparently they've
taken some kind of vacation,

50
00:03:53,652 --> 00:03:55,240
both of them went overseas since yesterday.

51
00:03:55,620 --> 00:03:57,960
You've got to be kidding me,
at a time like this!

52
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,780
Yes, this is Nakagawa.

53
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,720
Senpai!

54
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,640
It's urgent! Get back here right away!

55
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,660
Well, you see...

56
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:13,580
I heard there's been trouble at the
resource survey site in the Amazon,

57
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,860
and I'm on my way there now,

58
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:18,800
but I'm deep in the jungle where
even helicopters can't reach,

59
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,740
so I can't move anywhere right away.

60
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:22,940
Senpai?

61
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:25,000
Yes, this is Eiko.

62
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,500
Ryo-chan. What's wrong?

63
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,900
You're asking if I can get
back to Japan right away?

64
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,400
Of course that's impossible, you know.

65
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,900
It's already winter in Antarctica now.

66
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,920
Why don't you come over here, Ryo-chan?

67
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,620
Damn, these useless good-for-nothings
when it really counts!

68
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:45,260
Without those two,
Hawaii is out of the question.

69
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:47,500
Maybe we should just return
the money after all...

70
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:50,260
Wait, wait,
there must still be some other way.

71
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:51,620
Is Ryo-san here?

72
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,560
Oh, it's just Hirami's old granny.

73
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,420
Not now, I'm busy!

74
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,320
Later, later!

75
00:04:59,320 --> 00:04:59,844
Well, you see,

76
00:04:59,894 --> 00:05:04,060
I heard that thanks to Ryo-san,
we're going to Hawaii.

77
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:08,880
I made some simmered taro as a
small offering for the spirits.

78
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,540
What, the news has already spread?

79
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,880
The information network is frightening.

80
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,700
S-senpai!

81
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,300
These are pickles I've been
brining for a whole year.

82
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,360
How about some takikomi rice?

83
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,160
These are fresh vegetables
sent to us by relatives.

84
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,820
We're counting on you, Ryo-san.

85
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:31,020
After all, it's an overseas trip.

86
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:33,680
It's my first time traveling abroad,
you know.

87
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,980
That's right.

88
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:38,500
So I've been really
looking forward to this trip.

89
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,780
Please, Ryo-san.

90
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,580
So it's your first time?

91
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,020
Rest assured.

92
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:48,400
We at Ryotsu Tourism will
get you all safely to Hawaii.

93
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,800
"We"?

94
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,160
Us too.

95
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,780
It's for the citizens.

96
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:55,540
You'll cooperate, of course, right?

97
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:57,140
Of course.

98
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,360
That's how it is.

99
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:02,160
Rest easy and leave it
to us at Ryotsu Tourism.

100
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:05,980
Great, now we'll have
souvenirs to bring back!

101
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,060
Thank you, thank you.

102
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:10,020
Thank you, thank you.

103
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:12,660
Leave it to me.

104
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,960
It's really too reckless, after all.

105
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:22,780
How are we supposed to take 20
people to Hawaii with 500,000 yen?

106
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:25,440
You don't really mean to
make us pay for it, do you?

107
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:29,500
I still have 19 years left on my house loan,
you know.

108
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:32,340
Who was ever counting on your money,
you dumbass?

109
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:34,440
All we need is for you to lend a hand.

110
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:37,880
Now, I'll explain the
details of this trip plan.

111
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,960
Here's a map of Hawaii.

112
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:44,500
Ryo-sama, this is a map of the Kanto region!

113
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,640
Look closely, Hawaii's right here!

114
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:52,040
That's Kanagawa, though.

115
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:59,640
I've heard there's another place called Hawaii,
far off across the Pacific Ocean.

116
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:03,880
But the road to get there
is extremely difficult...

117
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:07,120
Even on the Kanrin Maru,
it'd take forty days...

118
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:08,740
Everyone!

119
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,840
With the elderly's stamina,
it's simply impossible.

120
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:19,560
So we've had no choice but
to go to a nearby Hawaii.

121
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:22,080
I had a bad feeling about this.

122
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:26,700
Joking aside, how could we deceive
those elderly folks like that?

123
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:29,400
Everyone's been looking
forward to that Hawaii trip!

124
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,720
Would you trample on the dreams of old
people with only a night or two left to live?

125
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:36,220
Taking them to a fake Hawaii would be far crueler,
don't you think?

126
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,860
I won't cooperate.

127
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,040
What is this?

128
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:44,720
Isn't this the non-sale phone
card Saori gave me the other day?

129
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:47,620
I was going to give it to someone,
but who was it again?

130
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:53,100
Some elderly people might be shocked
to learn the trip was canceled.

131
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:56,140
Let's at least give them
the feeling of a Hawaii trip.

132
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:58,040
I see, so you understand now.

133
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,320
I'll help too, if it's for you, Ryo-sama.

134
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,460
Through fire and water.

135
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:05,920
Alright, let's all stage a fun Hawaii trip!

136
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:07,180
Yah!

137
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,920
I was so excited last
night I couldn't sleep.

138
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,640
It's our dream Hawaii, after all.

139
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,880
But it's all thanks to Ryo-san.

140
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:22,840
Here they come!

141
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:32,000
Alright, sorry to keep you waiting,
senior citizens' association!

142
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,400
Ryo-san!

143
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,920
We've been waiting for you.

144
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:36,060
Nice to meet you, we're in your care.

145
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:40,120
Now, I'll be guiding you
all on your trip to Hawaii.

146
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:54,940
Thank you for your long wait.

147
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,980
We will arrive at Narita Airport shortly.

148
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:13,040
Behold!

149
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:17,600
This is the super jumbo that
will take you all to Hawaii.

150
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:20,880
What a fine souvenir, dear.

151
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:22,600
Thank you, thank you.

152
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:26,320
Hey, hey, it looks totally
different from the photo, though.

153
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:28,560
W-what are you talking about?

154
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:32,380
See? It has a fuselage,
main wings, and a tail fin.

155
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:34,460
Isn't it exactly the same?

156
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:37,640
But the photo here
doesn't show any propellers.

157
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:41,100
Well, that's because they spin at high speed,
so they don't show up in photos.

158
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:46,120
You probably don't know this, since you
don't get many chances to ride on airplanes,

159
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,200
but modern jet airliners

160
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,600
have propellers attached

161
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,760
to stabilize the airflow
near the main wings.

162
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:54,240
That's common knowledge.

163
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,720
I see. As expected of Ryo-san.

164
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,000
You really know your stuff.

165
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,220
Please watch your step as you board.

166
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,400
Welcome, welcome to Tokyo... "Tōkī"!

167
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:10,200
The stewardesses are certainly pretty,
as expected.

168
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,060
Oops, sorry, sorry.

169
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,660
My legs got tangled up, you see.

170
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,740
You should be more careful.

171
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:20,780
Still, you've got a nice, firm behind.

172
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,260
Stop it, Grandpa!

173
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:24,640
My hand slipped.

174
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,000
Otome Maida.

175
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,400
Pachikura Mida.

176
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:32,600
If those guys find out Maria's a man,
they might die of shock.

177
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,080
This flight will depart
Narita Airport shortly

178
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:39,280
and head for Honolulu Airport in Hawaii.

179
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,760
Ladies and gentlemen,
please fasten your seatbelts.

180
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,780
Is that all?

181
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,840
It's basically like volunteer work.

182
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:52,300
We should be grateful
just to get paid at all.

183
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:54,520
Chief!

184
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:59,440
The customers say they'd like
the Chief to say a few words.

185
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,260
What?

186
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:04,060
Didn't the Chief say a
few words before departure?

187
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:06,440
Wait, I'm coming!

188
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,480
I wonder what's keeping the Chief.

189
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,100
He's probably busy.

190
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,520
Sorry to keep you waiting.

191
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,540
I'm Captain Gyakufunsha Hachitaro.

192
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:16,520
Nice to meet you.

193
00:11:16,970 --> 00:11:18,040
The pleasure is mine.

194
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:23,700
Excuse me, Captain.

195
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:25,320
Yes, yes, what is it?

196
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:27,760
Could you call Ryo-san for me?

197
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,980
Yes, understood.

198
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:31,080
You there, Chief!

199
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,020
Yes, do you need something?

200
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:37,525
Ryo-san,

201
00:11:37,575 --> 00:11:41,340
could you ask the captain
how long until we reach Hawaii?

202
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:42,860
Hehe.

203
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,860
Apparently the captain's
flight time is almost up.

204
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:50,160
Yes, this is the captain.
It's a six-hour flight.

205
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,560
I can't hear you clearly, though.

206
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:56,580
Sorry, but could you come out over here?

207
00:11:56,580 --> 00:12:00,380
It may vary a bit depending on the air currents,
but it's about six hours.

208
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,720
Ryo-san, where do we show our passports?

209
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:04,580
I've taken care of it on my end.

210
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:06,520
You don't need to show them at all.

211
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:07,800
By the way, Captain.

212
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,160
Yes, what is it?

213
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,520
No, never mind, Ryo-san.

214
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,440
Yeah, yeah.

215
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:14,300
Captain? Ryo-san?

216
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,900
What do you want?

217
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,160
What was it again?

218
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,000
I can't keep doing this forever!
Let's take off, Maria!

219
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:23,680
Yes, Ryo-sama.

220
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:25,740
Are you ready?

221
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:27,040
We're good to go.

222
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,360
We're all set over here too.

223
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:35,180
Ah this is the captain's reverse car.

224
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:37,460
We're now taking off.

225
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:40,560
It's moving!

226
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:49,580
You asked to borrow a plane being dismantled,
so I wondered what you'd use it for.

227
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,920
Can we really fool anyone with this?

228
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:15,780
Come on, roll more quietly,
like a real airplane!

229
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:17,680
Don't be unreasonable!

230
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,300
We'll be a bit bumpy until
we reach cruising altitude,

231
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,180
so please bear with us for a while.

232
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:25,640
You can't even read the guidebook.

233
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,920
Please don't look outside during the climb.

234
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:35,700
There's neon right nearby now -

235
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:38,860
No, that's an early
symptom of neon sickness!

236
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,000
Neon sickness?

237
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:43,420
That illness wasn't in the guidebook.

238
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:44,460
It's a real thing.

239
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,320
If you keep staring out the
window of a climbing plane,

240
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:49,540
things on the ground
start looking strangely big,

241
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:53,880
and eventually you start seeing things that aren't there,
like pink elephants and white crocodiles.

242
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,700
It's a terrifying illness.

243
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,380
Such an illness exists?

244
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:00,600
You're still fine for now.

245
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,960
Just close your eyes for
a while and it'll go away.

246
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,320
Whoa, that's scary!

247
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,100
What's the matter?

248
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:16,840
We seem to keep stopping
since a while ago, though.

249
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:19,320
We got caught in a traffic jam.

250
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:21,540
The planes are jammed up.

251
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:24,940
Don't talk nonsense, Grandpa.

252
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,540
And the traffic lights too.

253
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:31,080
No, it only feels like we've
stopped because of the headwind.

254
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,880
That's common knowledge about Super Jumbos.

255
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:37,340
Besides, this area is off-limits
to anyone but staff, you know.

256
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:39,220
Please go back to your seat.

257
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:40,840
Sorry about that.

258
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,140
Yeah.

259
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:45,740
Hand out the food and keep
their minds on the eating.

260
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:48,740
While you're at it,
pour plenty of sake and put them to sleep.

261
00:14:49,110 --> 00:14:50,640
Understood, Lord Ryo.

262
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:55,980
Thank you all for your patience.
It's time for your meal.

263
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:57,680
Here you go.

264
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,820
So this is the in-flight meal.

265
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,900
I've never seen one before.
Living long really is worth it.

266
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,720
Hurry up and pass some over here too.

267
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,440
Coming right up!

268
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,900
Did Maria make this by hand?

269
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:11,340
It should taste better than
the real in-flight meal.

270
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:12,820
This is delicious!

271
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,160
Living long really is worth it.

272
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:15,720
We're so grateful, so grateful.

273
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,920
Well, well, would anyone like some sake?

274
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:18,900
We've been waiting for this!

275
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:22,160
Anyway, we have plenty of
time until we reach Hawaii.

276
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,840
Please keep drinking, don't hold back.

277
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:37,920
Those old men and women are a real handful,
but at least we can catch our breath now.

278
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:50,460
Looks like we got caught after all.

279
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:55,380
Neon sick, neon sick.

280
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,700
What? Rain?

281
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:05,080
Hey, who am I to say anything?

282
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,200
They're making a fool of us!

283
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:11,220
Stop it.

284
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:18,000
Aim for it, shake them off no matter what!

285
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,060
That's impossible.

286
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,380
Consider it a lesson.

287
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:31,100
Brother.

288
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:39,260
Zzzt! We're up in the sky now.

289
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,740
We have just entered turbulence.

290
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:44,000
Please fasten your seatbelts securely.

291
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,820
Turbulence! It's turbulence!

292
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:54,600
It's an air pocket!

293
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,020
What's going on?

294
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:03,620
Take us to Miura Beach, please.

295
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,700
We're here.

296
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,640
How's the preparation?

297
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,100
Everything's perfect.

298
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:24,020
With this, it'll look like
Hawaii from any angle, right?

299
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:27,940
Even the beach hut is here, see?

300
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,460
Good, that's excellent work.

301
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,820
Everyone, we've arrived in Hawaii.

302
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:40,320
Come on,
wake up quickly and get ready to disembark.

303
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:43,620
Have we really arrived in Hawaii?

304
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:45,720
You're not pulling a fast one on us,
are you?

305
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:51,640
Here we are, the Hawaii of your dreams!

306
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,760
Why are we included too?

307
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,800
Living long really pays off.

308
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:02,360
Stepping off and straight onto the beach,
America really is something else.

309
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:06,920
Welcome to Hawaii!

310
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:09,720
Living long really pays off.

311
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:12,200
Welcome to Hawaii!

312
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,960
Foreigners really are something,
with those big bodies.

313
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,920
I'll carry this one for you.

314
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,700
What's wrong?

315
00:18:19,900 --> 00:18:21,240
No way, no way, no way!

316
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,574
Saori, please forgive me.

317
00:18:26,624 --> 00:18:28,920
I'm doing all of this for your sake.

318
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,180
What are you talking about?

319
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:05,240
Just hurry up and get
back to the police box.

320
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,280
Karakiru gēshō fujijaba

321
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:10,120
That was close.

322
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,800
When you come to a tourist spot overseas,

323
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,920
people pose as acquaintances
and approach you like that,

324
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,100
there are crooks who steal your luggage.

325
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:18,320
Everyone, please be very careful.

326
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:21,140
Though he really did look
a lot like that person.

327
00:19:22,380 --> 00:19:23,020
Well then, everyone,

328
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,520
let's take you on a tour
of the Hawaiian sights.

329
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:32,840
Truly a magnificent view.

330
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:34,940
A sight you can't see in Japan.

331
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,980
It's worth living a long life, isn't it.

332
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:40,240
But there seem to be an awful
lot of Japanese people here.

333
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:44,880
Recently, every tourist spot
is packed with Japanese people.

334
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,660
That's Diamond Head,
the one that's sung about in songs.

335
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:50,640
It's shaped like a diamond, right?

336
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:53,020
I can sing that song, you know.

337
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:56,780
It looks more like Enoshima
than a diamond, though.

338
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:59,820
We get people who say that all the time.

339
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:02,640
And this is the statue of King Kamehameha.

340
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:06,520
So the Hawaiian king also had a topknot.

341
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:09,380
It's quite different from the photos.

342
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:11,460
This one is an old piece.

343
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,620
It was restored to this
form after the war, really.

344
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:16,000
That's Kilauea volcano.

345
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,540
This is Pearl Harbor.

346
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:20,140
These days, when you think of Hawaii,
you think of weddings.

347
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:24,300
And your accommodation tonight is here,
the Royal Hawaiian Hotel.

348
00:20:25,380 --> 00:20:29,040
Now, please enjoy the Hawaiian delicacies
to your heart's content tonight.

349
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,200
Thank you for the meal.

350
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:37,080
Sashimi and tempura!
Do they have things like this in Hawaii too?

351
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:39,960
It's sashimi of tropical fish
and tempura of Maui shrimp.

352
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,580
It's a specialty of Hawaii, you know.

353
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,680
Excuse me.

354
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:48,060
I told you to create a Hawaiian atmosphere,
didn't I?

355
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:49,840
Even though you say that...

356
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:50,460
That's...

357
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,560
Here's the hot pot.

358
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,180
Sir, what are you going to do?

359
00:20:59,180 --> 00:21:00,220
Shut up!

360
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:04,180
It's Hawaii's famous tropical hot pot,
with all these fruits thrown in!

361
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:07,060
See, it looks so delicious, doesn't it?

362
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:11,080
So there's a Hawaiian hot pot

363
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,780
It's so delicious, so delicious!

364
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:17,360
The pineapple and fish stock create a wonderful harmony,
don't they?

365
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,840
You can really eat this, can't you?

366
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:22,480
That's because they completely
believe it's Hawaiian cuisine.

367
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,700
No matter what you say,
we can't go any further than this.

368
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:30,900
Damn it, this is a disaster. If that's the case,
then this, that, and this adds up to...

369
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:38,340
This is completely over budget!
My profit margin is in the red!

370
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:39,380
Yō-sama.

371
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,300
What is it, Maria?

372
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,940
Everyone wants to see a fire dance.

373
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:48,360
A fire dance?
There's no way we can do that at a banquet!

374
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:51,400
But everyone's totally fired up.

375
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,280
This is desperate now.

376
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,260
You're making good use of it.

377
00:21:58,260 --> 00:21:59,400
Finally, we've been waiting!

378
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:23,180
The passion of my youth is coming back!

379
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,860
Alright, me too!

380
00:22:27,860 --> 00:22:28,640
Me too.

381
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:29,300
I want a turn too!

382
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:35,440
Me, me!

383
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:36,680
Me, me!

384
00:22:37,620 --> 00:22:38,480
Ryo-sama?

385
00:22:42,020 --> 00:22:43,080
Nyahahaha!

386
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:45,960
Me!

387
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:46,820
Hahaha!

388
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:47,920
Me, me!

389
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:48,940
Me, me!

390
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:02,360
You bloody idiot!

391
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:05,440
What kind of man are you!

392
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:09,820
No one was hurt,
so that's good enough, right?

393
00:23:10,580 --> 00:23:12,020
That's beside the point!

394
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:16,600
How did the senior citizens who were supposed to
be in Hawaii end up looking like the Miura group!

395
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,300
There's a deep reason for that.

396
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,920
Is Ryo-san here?

397
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:24,980
E-everyone...

398
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:26,401
W-well, everyone,

399
00:23:26,451 --> 00:23:29,720
I'm truly sorry for this idiot's

400
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:33,140
Why are you apologizing?
We came today to thank you.

401
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:36,700
That was really a fun trip.

402
00:23:36,700 --> 00:23:39,840
It's been a long time
since we made such a ruckus.

403
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:41,480
Wow, we've gotten younger.

404
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:44,220
But, well, Hawaii...

405
00:23:44,220 --> 00:23:47,280
What we went to was definitely Hawaii.

406
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:49,540
It was the Hawaii I'd dreamed of.

407
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:54,040
Let's go on another trip together, Ryo-san.

408
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:57,420
Next time, to Hawaii across the ocean.

409
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:10,140
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, a fourth grader.

410
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:13,100
The one who came to replace our homeroom teacher,
who was lured away by Ōtoyama Forest,

411
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,760
is a beautiful female teacher, no less!

412
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:16,060
Regional governor Toppe

413
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:17,740
Let's give them a big welcome.

414
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:20,340
Next time:
The Day the Obake Entotsu Disappeared

415
00:24:20,340 --> 00:24:21,420
Be sure to watch!

416
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:41,100
Surprise and commotion,
solved at just the right moment,

417
00:24:41,100 --> 00:24:49,880
quick to lend a hand,
a flash of inspiration in time.

418
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:55,720
Bouncing along and gathering together,
we take action and fly off.

419
00:24:56,660 --> 00:25:00,600
Above all, power for sumo!

420
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:06,480
Gather everyone, come here,

421
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:12,780
like a dream, the final energy.

422
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:17,120
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

423
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,040
painting the universe,
standing on the ground.

424
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,840
The Kameari star spun
around and drew a circle.

425
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:27,480
This should be good enough, right?

426
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:29,040
Like hell it is!

427
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

